Grammar

    0 $accept: file $end

    1 file: balise

    2 balise: '<' IDENTIFIER attribute_list '>' balise_list '<' '/' IDENTIFIER '>'
    3       | '<' IDENTIFIER attribute_list CONTENT '/' IDENTIFIER '>'

    4 balise_list: balise_list balise
    5            | ε

    6 attribute: IDENTIFIER '=' STRING

    7 attribute_list: attribute_list attribute
    8               | ε


Terminals, with rules where they appear

    $end (0) 0
    '/' (47) 2 3
    '<' (60) 2 3
    '=' (61) 6
    '>' (62) 2 3
    error (256)
    IDENTIFIER <vstring> (258) 2 3 6
    STRING <vstring> (259) 6
    CONTENT <vstring> (260) 3


Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

    $accept (10)
        on left: 0
    file (11)
        on left: 1
        on right: 0
    balise <vbalise> (12)
        on left: 2 3
        on right: 1 4
    balise_list <varray> (13)
        on left: 4 5
        on right: 2 4
    attribute <vattribute> (14)
        on left: 6
        on right: 7
    attribute_list <varray> (15)
        on left: 7 8
        on right: 2 3 7


State 0

    0 $accept: • file $end

    '<'  shift, and go to state 1

    file    go to state 2
    balise  go to state 3


State 1

    2 balise: '<' • IDENTIFIER attribute_list '>' balise_list '<' '/' IDENTIFIER '>'
    3       | '<' • IDENTIFIER attribute_list CONTENT '/' IDENTIFIER '>'

    IDENTIFIER  shift, and go to state 4


State 2

    0 $accept: file • $end

    $end  shift, and go to state 5


State 3

    1 file: balise •

    $default  reduce using rule 1 (file)


State 4

    2 balise: '<' IDENTIFIER • attribute_list '>' balise_list '<' '/' IDENTIFIER '>'
    3       | '<' IDENTIFIER • attribute_list CONTENT '/' IDENTIFIER '>'

    $default  reduce using rule 8 (attribute_list)

    attribute_list  go to state 6


State 5

    0 $accept: file $end •

    $default  accept


State 6

    2 balise: '<' IDENTIFIER attribute_list • '>' balise_list '<' '/' IDENTIFIER '>'
    3       | '<' IDENTIFIER attribute_list • CONTENT '/' IDENTIFIER '>'
    7 attribute_list: attribute_list • attribute

    IDENTIFIER  shift, and go to state 7
    CONTENT     shift, and go to state 8
    '>'         shift, and go to state 9

    attribute  go to state 10


State 7

    6 attribute: IDENTIFIER • '=' STRING

    '='  shift, and go to state 11


State 8

    3 balise: '<' IDENTIFIER attribute_list CONTENT • '/' IDENTIFIER '>'

    '/'  shift, and go to state 12


State 9

    2 balise: '<' IDENTIFIER attribute_list '>' • balise_list '<' '/' IDENTIFIER '>'

    $default  reduce using rule 5 (balise_list)

    balise_list  go to state 13


State 10

    7 attribute_list: attribute_list attribute •

    $default  reduce using rule 7 (attribute_list)


State 11

    6 attribute: IDENTIFIER '=' • STRING

    STRING  shift, and go to state 14


State 12

    3 balise: '<' IDENTIFIER attribute_list CONTENT '/' • IDENTIFIER '>'

    IDENTIFIER  shift, and go to state 15


State 13

    2 balise: '<' IDENTIFIER attribute_list '>' balise_list • '<' '/' IDENTIFIER '>'
    4 balise_list: balise_list • balise

    '<'  shift, and go to state 16

    balise  go to state 17


State 14

    6 attribute: IDENTIFIER '=' STRING •

    $default  reduce using rule 6 (attribute)


State 15

    3 balise: '<' IDENTIFIER attribute_list CONTENT '/' IDENTIFIER • '>'

    '>'  shift, and go to state 18


State 16

    2 balise: '<' • IDENTIFIER attribute_list '>' balise_list '<' '/' IDENTIFIER '>'
    2       | '<' IDENTIFIER attribute_list '>' balise_list '<' • '/' IDENTIFIER '>'
    3       | '<' • IDENTIFIER attribute_list CONTENT '/' IDENTIFIER '>'

    IDENTIFIER  shift, and go to state 4
    '/'         shift, and go to state 19


State 17

    4 balise_list: balise_list balise •

    $default  reduce using rule 4 (balise_list)


State 18

    3 balise: '<' IDENTIFIER attribute_list CONTENT '/' IDENTIFIER '>' •

    $default  reduce using rule 3 (balise)


State 19

    2 balise: '<' IDENTIFIER attribute_list '>' balise_list '<' '/' • IDENTIFIER '>'

    IDENTIFIER  shift, and go to state 20


State 20

    2 balise: '<' IDENTIFIER attribute_list '>' balise_list '<' '/' IDENTIFIER • '>'

    '>'  shift, and go to state 21


State 21

    2 balise: '<' IDENTIFIER attribute_list '>' balise_list '<' '/' IDENTIFIER '>' •

    $default  reduce using rule 2 (balise)
